-- erwartet: P014
-- **The AMBIGUOUS one of the eight attempts** (`PLAN-HARDWARE.md` §49 B3, attempt 2 of 8) --
-- and the calculation says KEEP the refusal.
--
-- The test is: what becomes sayable, and is it wrong? `effects { }` would mean "this
-- function has no effects", and that meaning already EXISTS and is spelled `effects
-- { pure }`. Two spellings for one meaning, one of which nobody reads -- and `E001` calls
-- the missing clause *"at once the strongest promise and the cheapest one to write"*, which
-- is exactly the reason the promise must be WRITTEN and not left as an empty pair of braces.
--
-- **What was a paper cut was the MESSAGE, and only that.** It read `effect expected, `}`
-- found` and listed the nine effect words -- leaving the reader to work out which of the
-- nine means "none". It now names the substitute.
module m {
impl fn addiere(a : u32 in 0 .. 100, b : u32 in 0 .. 100) -> u32 in 0 .. 200
    effects { } costs <= 3 ops
{
    return a + b;
}
}
